This directory contains the source code for NDI, a nuclear data
interface.


BUILDING NDI

To build NDI you must specify a configuration.  Available
configuration files are in directory conf/.

For example
    make CONFIG=intel-linux
will build optimized and debug versions of the library placing the
output (and associated build tree) in
    build-intel-linux/
and
    debug-intel-linux/


Other targets:

make distclean                        - removes all build trees

make CONFIG=intel-linux build         - builds the optimized tree only

make CONFIG=intel-linux debug         - builds the debug tree only

make CONFIG=intel-linux clean         - removes intermediate files

make CONFIG=intel-linux clean-build   - removes intermediate files
                                        from the optimized tree

make CONFIG=intel-linux clean-debug   - removes intermediate files
                                        from the debug tree

make CONFIG=intel-linux check         - builds (and runs) tests

make CONFIG=intel-linux check-build   - builds (and runs) tests
                                        in the optimized tree

make CONFIG=intel-linux check-debug   - builds (and runs) tests
                                        in the debug tree


make CONFIG=intel-linux prefix=... install
                                      - installs the opimized library
        

make CONFIG=intel-linux prefix=... install-debug
                                      - installs the debug library
